Patch 0002 of the ztOS camera-application candidates. Target:
ztmetro/camera/ztcamera.c at ztOS
94b35c2a1f4ceb568bc0ab60f5a1acebe7cfefaf, the pinned upstream revision.

Base: the accepted composed delta 0001 applied, i.e. source sha256
166d8d0490d328cf14ef7d173531eb9f24d94b7bb8450b64e2bb4ed566cacab0, the source
of the installed application.
Result: source sha256
5647a698e1db38b0af0c911a3ad2a0df1576c69bd9dbab3a6d7645dbcb17ebee.

Apply after 0001, from the ztOS checkout's `ztmetro/` directory, with GNU
`patch` (the diff paths are relative to that directory, as in the local camera
kit); the header above is skipped by patch:

    cd ztmetro
    patch -p1 -F0 < ../patches/userspace/ztcamera/0002-sensor-720p30-cap.patch

Effect: after STREAMON, on `s5k3l8` only and only when the VBLANK control's
maximum is 0xffff-720, writes V4L2_CID_VBLANK 2530 (VTS 3250, 29.8 fps) and
re-reads the exposure range, which widens to 1/30 s (804 -> 3242 lines). The
same file applied to the camera-v3 line gives the accepted 720p30 source
0742a21d.

Status: candidate, not accepted state. Host-verified: applies to the published
chain without fuzz and reproduces the source hash above. The candidate build
that contains it (vblank + AF settle) was built twice byte-identically and
passed the artifact check host-side; it was never run on the phone and is not
installed.

